  "content": {
    "body": "## Skill pebble anatomy (content kind \"skill\")\n\n`purpose` (one line) · `whenToUse` (trigger conditions) · `arguments`\n(what the invocation accepts, e.g. \"$ARGUMENTS\") · `prerequisites[]` ·\n`tools` (allowed tools, empty = unrestricted) · `steps[]` (the ordered\nprocedure — for system skills these ARE the prompt body) ·\n`constraints[]` (hard must/never rules) · `output` (definition of\ndone) · `examples[]` (input→output pairs).\n\n## How a /command executes\n\nTyping \"/name args\" in chat expands the skill body: `$ARGUMENTS` is\nreplaced with the typed args (appended when no placeholder), and\n`{PEBBLES_CLI}` is replaced with the real CLI path at send time. The\nexpanded body rides the relay like a user message, under the full\ncontract. The chat runs the PEBBLE's current content — editing a system\nskill's steps changes the /command immediately.\n\n## System skills (skills/system/ — edit-only, restorable, self-healing)\n\nUnderstanding: /pebbles-discover — settle intent + spec readiness\nBEFORE any work (read-only; the understand-before-acting rule applies\nits essence implicitly to every task).\nRead/explore: /pebbles-sections · /pebbles-list · /pebbles-get ·\n/pebbles-query · /pebbles-refs · /pebbles-validate\nCode graph: /pebbles-map · /pebbles-find-code\nWrite/bind: /pebbles-create · /pebbles-update · /pebbles-set-status ·\n/pebbles-add-item · /pebbles-link-code\nSpec↔code loops: /pebbles-verify · /pebbles-fix · /pebbles-investigate\n· /pebbles-sync-model\nReverse mode: /pebbles-shallow-extract (overview milestones) ·\n/pebbles-extract (one topic, single level, exhaustive) ·\n/pebbles-deep-extract (multi-level with reconciliation) ·\n/pebbles-onboard (whole app onboarding)\nAnalysis/health: /pebbles-audit · /pebbles-coverage · /pebbles-impact ·\n/pebbles-plan · /pebbles-report\n\nEach system skill carries graph refs to the system RULES that govern it\nand the KNOWLEDGE concepts it depends on. Identity (name/title/\nfilename) is locked — the /command and restore mapping key off it; only\nthe content is editable. Deleted out-of-band → recreated from factory\nwithin seconds. Restore (sidebar ↺) rewrites all from factory, ids\npreserved, user skills untouched.\n\n## User skills\n\nAny skill pebble OUTSIDE skills/system/ becomes a /command\nautomatically (name = filename stem). Saved harness skills are also\ndiscovered and offered in the picker:\n\n| Source | Project scope | User scope |\n|---|---|---|\n| Claude Code | .claude/commands, .claude/skills | ~/.claude/commands, ~/.claude/skills |\n| Codex | — | ~/.codex/prompts |\n| OpenCode | .opencode/command | ~/.config/opencode/command |\n| Custom | folders configured in Settings | — |\n\nName collisions: the active harness's own skill wins, then custom\nfolders, then other harnesses. A skill saved for one harness works when\nchatting with ANY harness — Pebbles expands the file itself.\n\n## Agents\n\nAgent pebbles are specialist PERSONAS: role (one line), persona\n(expertise and method — not procedure), boundaries (out-of-scope +\nwrite posture), escalation (hand-offs), hard constraints. Their\nskills/rules/knowledge ride as graph refs and resolve into the prompt\nwhen the agent is selected in chat. Persona OVERLAYS procedure: the\nagent supplies judgment, boundaries and voice; an invoked skill's\nsteps remain authoritative — a persona may sharpen a procedure, never\nskip it.\n\nThe system roster (agents/system/ — edit-only, restorable):\nplatform-oracle (knows everything, answers with evidence, routes to\nspecialists) · data-modeler (models, FKs, schema drift) · implementer\n(spec → code, honestly statused) · workflow (extracts AND verifies\nworkflow pebbles — walks code flow node-by-node, both directions) · architect\n(boundaries, blast radius, large-change plans) · verifier (independent\nQA; never implements — findings, statuses, coverage only) · sentinel\n(security/integrity audits; findings-only). Every agent declares what\nit does NOT do and to whom it hands off — overlap prevention is what\nmakes a roster a system.",
    "kind": "text"
  },
